hordeshooter (working title): credits and licences

Code: this repository (MIT, see LICENSE). Every texture, model, colour grade,
effect sheet and sound is generated by this game's own code; no third-party art
or audio is shipped, so there is nothing further to attribute.

Where each asset comes from
- assets/models/*.cwchar (the soldier, the four creatures, the wall, masts,
  containers, barriers, rubble, tyres, pipes): modelled and animated by
  tools/blender/hordechars.py and tools/blender/hordeprops.py, run headless in
  Blender (Blender is used as a tool; its output is ours). Rerun them to
  rebuild the files.
- assets/grade/dusk.cube: tools/gen-lut.mjs.
- The descent's levels (LEVELS.md): assets/levels/*.cwlevel and their lighting
  scenes assets/scenes/<level>.cwscene from tools/gen-levels.mjs; the floors
  assets/textures/*_floor.png from tools/gen-level-textures.mjs; the grades
  assets/grade/<level>.cube from tools/gen-level-luts.mjs; the monsters and
  bosses (assets/models/<level>_*.cwchar) from tools/blender/levelchars.py; the
  props, hatches, gun pickups and the loot cache from tools/blender/levelprops.py;
  the bakes assets/lightmaps/<level>.cwlm from the hordeshooter_levelview build
  (LEVEL_BAKE). All generated by this game's code; no outside art.
- assets/fx/fire.png, fire_mv.png, smoke.png, smoke_mv.png, scorch.png (fire
  and smoke flipbooks with their motion-vector sheets, the scorch shapes):
  baked by cartwheel-engine's tools/fx/bake-flipbooks.mjs (procedural, CC0,
  listed in the engine's NOTICE): node <engine>/tools/fx/bake-flipbooks.mjs assets/fx
- assets/fx/haze.png (the heat-haze swirl): tools/gen-fx-sheets.mjs.
- Surface textures (floor, crates, walls, skin, plate): generated at start-up by
  view.c from integer hashes.
- Sounds: synthesised in main.c.

Engine: cartwheel-engine (MIT) with three.c; the crowd is Recast and Detour
(zlib) and RVO2 (Apache-2.0), see the engine's NOTICE.

Fonts: the engine's built-in sans (see the engine's NOTICE for its licence).

Design reading (nothing copied): Red Blob Games, "Flow Field Pathfinding for
Tower Defense" (https://redblobgames.com/pathfinding/tower-defense).
